  "synthesis": {
    "description": "A coordinator asks the team to submit their planned vacation for the coming month, or a staff member confirms their own days. People announce when they will be out and list who covers each of their duties, such as error reports or sending nominations, or name one colleague to handle the whole desk. A manager approves short-notice time off and asks that longer vacations be raised in advance.",
    "steps": [
      "The coordinator asks staff to submit the coming month's vacation dates.",
      "Staff send or confirm their vacation days.",
      "The manager approves the time off.",
      "The absent person announces the dates and names who covers each duty."
    ],
    "approach": "A shared team calendar with a time-off request form that captures dates and a coverage assignment for each duty, sending the approval and the coverage announcement from the same entry.",
    "rationale": "Each round gathers the same fields: dates, approval, and who covers which task. A form with a coverage table makes sure every duty has a named cover and saves rebuilding the list each time.",
    "artifact_type": "template"
  },
